1. e4 e5 2. f4 {"Leonard Barden suggested that Hartston tackle Spassky with
his own weapon. We (BH Wood?) feel Hartston contributed to the debacle which
followed rather more than Barden." (CHESS)} exf4 3. Nf3 d5 ({Spassky said
afterwards that he had seriously considered} 3... g5 {or Fischer's 3...d6.}) 4.
exd5 Nf6 5. Bb5+ ({Spassky smahes this. The old line} 5. c4 c6 6. d4 cxd5 7.
Bxf4 {may revert to favour.}) 5... c6 6. dxc6 Nxc6 ({Spassky's opponents in
simuls had done so well with this against him he had decided to try it himself.
} 6... bxc6 {is usual.}) 7. d4 Bd6 8. Qe2+ Be6 9. Ne5 O-O 10. Bxc6 bxc6 11.
Bxf4 Nd5 12. Bg3 f6 13. Nf3 Bxg3+ 14. hxg3 Re8 15. Kf2 Bf5 16. Qc4 Kh8 17. Nc3
Ne3 18. Qc5 Ng4+ 19. Kg1 Qd7 20. Rf1 Bxc2 21. Rh4 Ne3 22. Rc1 g5 23. Rh6 Bg6
24. Na4 Ng4 25. Rh3 Qe6 26. Qc3 Qxa2 27. Nc5 Re3 28. Qd2 Rae8 {Sources: The
Times, 6 January 1966; CHESS, January 1966, Vol.31/498-9, p146; BCM, February
1966, p35; BCM, March 1966, p70} 0-1

