Bd7 21. c3 a5 22. Rhd1 ({ChessBase version:} 22. Rad1) 22... Rhe8 23. Nf3 Re7
24. Nd2 b5 25. Nf3 Rae8 26. Re1 a4 27. b4 Bc6 28. Nd4 Bd7 29. Nf3 Re4 30. Rad1
{Here the ChessBase inputter, faced with the move 30 QR-Q1 in the score (which
is correct) but with a rook already on d1 as a result of the erroneous 22 Rad1,
improvises the move 30 Rd4.} R8e7 31. Rd5 Bc6 32. Rd4 g5 33. Rxe4 Rxe4 34. Nd4
Bd7 35. Kf3 Re8 36. Kf2 Kg6 37. Nc2 Re4 38. Rd1 Bc6 39. Nd4 Be8 40. Nc2 Bf7 41.
