{"Westerinen sacrificed a little too light-heartedly." (Editorial comment -
but wrong: the sacrifice is sound but the follow-up was incorrect - JS)} 23...
Qa5 $2 24. Nxh7 $1 $18 Kxh7 25. Nf3 $4 ({Move order disaster:} 25. Rf4 $1 $18
Kg8 (25... Bh6 26. Rh4 {and the threat of Rxh6+ and Qh4 mate is decisive}) 26.
Nf3 Qxc3 27. Qh4 {and the threat of Ng5 and Qh7 mate costs Black his queen.})
25... Bh6 $1 26. Ng5+ Bxg5 27. Qxg5 Rh8 28. Rf4 Kg8 29. Rh4 Rxh4 30. Qxh4 c4
31. Re3 Qc5 32. Qh6 Qf8 33. Qh4 Rb8 34. h3 Rb2 35. Kh2 Bf5 36. Rg3 Rb1 37. Re3
Be4 38. a4 Ra1 39. Re2 Qb8 40. Qf4 Rxa4 41. h4 Ra3 42. Re3 Ra2 43. Rg3 Rxg2+
44. Rxg2 Bxg2 45. Kxg2 Qb2+ 46. Kf3 Qxc3+ 47. Kg4 Qc2 48. h5 gxh5+ $6 {"and
meandered along to a 63-move win." Source: CHESS, March 1966, Vol.31/502, p217}
(48... Qg2+ 49. Kh4 g5+ 50. Qxg5+ Qxg5+ 51. Kxg5 c3 $19) 0-1

