1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 dxc3 5. Bc4 d6 6. Nxc3 Be6 7. Bxe6 fxe6 8.
Qb3 Qc8 (8... Qd7 {is an unsound sacrifice - Wise.}) 9. Ng5 Nd8 10. f4 Be7 11.
f5 $1 ({A pawn sacrifice invented recently by the Russians. Hoogendoorn plays
this line because Euwe only mentions} 11. O-O Bxg5 12. fxg5 Ne7 13. Nb5 e5 14.
Qc4 Nec6 {with advantage to Black, e.g.} 15. g6 hxg6 16. Bg5 a6 17. Bxd8 axb5
18. Qf7+ Kxd8) 11... Bxg5 ({If} 11... exf5 12. O-O $1 {with a very strong
attack.}) ({Stockfish 16:} 11... Nf6 12. O-O c6 13. fxe6 h6 14. Nf7 O-O {
is equal according to the engine, but White has kingside threats that might
well scare a human defender, e.g.} 15. e5 dxe5 16. Rxf6 gxf6 17. Nxh6+ Kh8 18.
Qd1 {, etc. JS}) 12. Bxg5 Nf6 (12... Nf7 13. fxe6 $1 Nxg5 14. Qb5+ c6 15. Qxg5
g6 16. O-O Qxe6 17. Nd5 $3 {with a winning attack.}) 13. Bxf6 gxf6 14. O-O e5
15. Nd5 Rf8 16. Qh3 c6 17. Qh5+ Kd7 18. Qxh7+ Nf7 ({If} 18... Rf7 19. Nxf6+ Ke7
20. Ng8+ Kf8 21. Qh8 {and wins.}) 19. Nxf6+ Kc7 20. Qg7 Kb6 21. Nh7 {Sources:
CHESS, March 1966, Vol.31/502, p216; Chessman Quarterly, Vol.3 No.16, Jan/Feb
1971, p168} 1-0

